<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<module fritzingVersion="1.0.2" moduleId="giovi321-hackaday-communicator-badge-mainboard-back_v2">
 <version>1.2</version>
 <author>giovi321 (geometry: Hack-a-Day, MIT)</author>
 <title>Hackaday Communicator Badge - main board (back view)</title>
 <label>BADGE</label>
 <date>2026-07-07</date>
 <description>Hackaday Supercon Communicator badge - main board, dimensionally accurate: 148 x 81 mm, generated from the official KiCad design (github.com/Hack-a-Day/2025-Communicator_Badge, MIT license).

Exposes the two expansion headers (plain through-holes on the stock badge) as connectors:
J8 - SAO v2 port, 2x3, 2.54 mm pitch, hole 1.016 mm: 3V3, GND, SDA (GPIO4), SCL (GPIO5), GPIO1 (GPIO7), GPIO2 (GPIO6).
J6 - expansion/GPS header, 1x4, 2.54 mm pitch, hole 1.0 mm: 3V3, IO11 (ESP TX), IO12 (ESP RX), GND.

BACK (battery-side) view, x mirrored, for add-on boards mounted on the back face. J8 pin 1 sits at (40.358, 9.596) mm from the back-view top-left corner; J6 pin 1 at (28.420, 6.040); J6-1 relative to J8-1: (-11.938, -3.556) mm = 4.7 x 1.4 pitches of 2.54 mm, so use a 0.254 mm grid when laying out a mating breakout. Watch back-side obstacles: the SX1262 module sits directly left of J6, the RST button below J8, and the ESP32-S3 module to the right; leave standoff height and keep RST reachable. The PCB view contains only the J8+J6 hole cluster at exact spacing, usable as a drill template. J7 (1x3 serial header) is drawn but not wired as a connector.</description>
 <tags><tag>hackaday</tag><tag>supercon</tag><tag>badge</tag><tag>SAO</tag><tag>ESP32-S3</tag><tag>LoRa</tag></tags>
 <properties>
  <property name="family">hackaday communicator badge</property>
  <property name="variant">main board, back view</property>
  <property name="layer"></property>
 </properties>
 <views>
  <iconView><layers image="icon/communicator-badge-mainboard_icon.svg"><layer layerId="icon"/></layers></iconView>
  <breadboardView><layers image="breadboard/communicator-badge-mainboard_breadboard.svg"><layer layerId="breadboard"/></layers></breadboardView>
  <schematicView><layers image="schematic/communicator-badge-mainboard_schematic.svg"><layer layerId="schematic"/></layers></schematicView>
  <pcbView><layers image="pcb/communicator-badge-mainboard_pcb.svg"><layer layerId="copper0"/><layer layerId="copper1"/><layer layerId="silkscreen"/></layers></pcbView>
 </views>
